deployment-time configuration flaw could introduce a manipulable pricing source 
even if the already-reviewed Vault logic is correct. EXIT CRITERIA: Trace every 
factory deployment path and initialization parameter into price-sensitive 
contracts; verify authorization, code validation, immutable/configured pricing 
dependencies, and any ability for untrusted callers to select or alter pools, 
routers, token indices, or strategies. Conclude with either a concrete 
price-manipulation attack path and affected deployments or evidence that all 
such configuration is trust-gated and constrained.

